			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">A couple of hours into the bumpy journey Bridgid and Devin's Tier'dal captors stopped at a camp of gypsies and traded out the ox cart for a shaggy pony.  They put her and Devin over the back of the beast and continued their pace even faster now with the pony trotting.  The ride was bumpy and Bridgid could feel the babe moving in protest.    It was still 3 weeks till she was due but as the night wore on and the cramps worsened Bridgid wondered if the babe were coming early.  She also wondered if dark elves could run all night.  
<br />

<br />
Apparently they could.  
<br />

<br />
As the sun crept over the horizon they crossed another river, then stopped and made camp in the shadows of a ridge.    She steeled her nerves thinking that now the dark elves would make sexual advances but instead they pulled her and Devin off the pony and ignored her.  
<br />

<br />
It took them three more days to cross the Karana beyond the river.  During the entire time Devin remained mostly unconscious.  Every time he started to awaken the dark elves beat him.  Bridgid knew they were moving southeast for Endah was at their backs, and Justica to their right.  But that was all she was able to discern.  The dark elves ignored her other than to give her food and drink.   They seemed very interested in keeping her alive which gave her some comfort.  Their eventual plans for her and Devin had her worried.    She remembered her mother telling her about the Neriak slave pits and especially about dark elf cruelty.  Was their lives now measured by their weight in copper?  Was that all they were now worth?   Bridgid sighed.  This was the start of a very long sad song.  If they ever made it to Surefall alive she'd have to compose a ballad.  Something to sing in the town's only tavern.  Something to sing in memory of Devin.  She glanced at his battered body.  She wasn't sure he'd survive.  It would be up to her to preserve his memory for their coming child.
<br />

<br />
On the eve of the fourth night they came to a great lake that sparkled like a gigantic blue jewel in the twilight.  The Tier'dal forced the pony into the water and they began swimming for a distant shore.  They swam for several hours and stopped at two islands along the way.  At one of them they slew a bird like creature and roasted it over an open fire.  They reached the far shore a couple of hours before morning and made camp off a mountain trail.  One of them went out for supplies while the others guarded her.  Devin was starting to awaken and Bridgid covered his face with the edge of her dress trying to stifle his moans.
<br />

<br />
The elf that went out for supplies returned to his companions and began speaking animatedly.  He pointed at her and Devin, said the words gypsies and Tier'dal half elf and held up three fingers.  Bridgid had a very bad feeling about what they were saying.  Especially when they separated her and Devin and drug him out into the middle of the mountain path and left him there.  They put a dagger to her throat  and drug her into the shadows.   Then they spread out along the brush and waited.  
<br />

<br />
They were setting a trap but for who and what, she didn't know and she didn't want to watch.  She only hoped whatever it was that it didn't make Devin suffer.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Kaldarye Ka'Duceus
