				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Vilamil looked down at the expanse of  the shimmering blue lake of Rathe with relief.  He was beginning to think the Rathe mountain range was unending and he'd be lost wandering the hills like that mad necromancer Kazzel.   He started sliding down the rocky trail towards the water.  The ground was wet with day old rain and he had to concentrate on his footing to keep from pitching over the edge.  It still several hundred feet to the water when a snap of brush caught his attention.  He stopped and  glanced in the direction of the sound, an outcropping of brownish rocks hanging precipatiously over the edge of a ravine.  The brush rattled again and  Vilamil crouched in a fighting stance,  only relaxing when a large colorful bird took flight from behind the rocks.  His gray eyes followed the bird as it  soared towards the water.  He supposed he was getting paranoid; this outdoor adventure was not to his liking.  He missed the city and it's familiar sounds and dangerous haunts.  As the bird dove into the lake he vowed this was the last time he was convincing D'Jaren he needed to travel anywhere near the mountains.   This wasn't even worth the 1000 pp he was getting paid, and he was tempted to go back to Greon's, fetch Kaldarye and turn her over to D'Jaren to pick up the whole 10,000 pp reward.   
<br />

<br />
As the bird flew off with a large silver fish, Vilamil continued towards the water.  Ahead of him the path went up a small incline then wrapped around a bend causing him to lose sight of the lake.  As the water came back into view  he was not prepared for what he saw.  A human, badly beaten lay in his path.   Vilamil stopped, knelt and checked for life.  The man was alive but needed help, which Vilamil had no intention of giving.  He searched the man's clothing for anything of value and finding nothing, not even a dagger for eating, he became suspicious.  He looked around and noticed the ridge above him was the perfect place to stage an ambush.  Not wanting to become the next victim of whatever attacked the human, Vilamil moved his hands to his daggers.  He studied his surroundings trying to figure which would be the most likely direction for an attack and concentrated on listening.  
<br />

<br />
The path and the ridge were silent.  So silent that Vilamil wondered if perhaps he was letting his imagination get the better of him.  Perhaps there was no impending attack and the human had crawled here from some other location.  He studied the path behind the man and saw several booted footprints.  But how old they were or even if they belonged to the human on the ground he had no idea.  He moved slowly away from the injured man, towards Lake Rathe, deciding it was better to trust his instincts and take caution.  The twang of a bow was his only warning that his earlier observation of an ambush had been correct.
<br />

<br />
The arrow bounced off the armor on his leg harmlessly.  He barely had time to register that the arrow was elven and that the shot was designed to maim not kill as dark elven assailants wearing red sashes broke their cover.  
<br />

<br />
Vilamil was unable to hide his shock.  His attackers were his own people. The Nerksis were in Rathe Mountains attacking him.  Was the world going insane.   Had these people caught the madness of Kazzel.  These thoughts flashed through his mind in the space of a second as more arrows bounced against his armor.
<br />

<br />
It didn't take him long to recover and now that he knew their position he sprang on the nearest assailant.  His right dagger cracked against the Tier'dal's bow while his left skewered the young elf's belly before the youngster could draw his melee weapon.  
<br />

<br />
As the first assailant sagged in a pool of blood, Vilamil dodged the overhead strike of the second.  This new assailant was older and more experienced.  He swung his offhand and Vilamil's dagger clashed with the sword.  Vilamil danced back and  tried to skewer this one in the belly as well but his opponent countered the stab with a clever parry that sent Vilamil leaping away.  Another round of arrows hit him and a lucky one found a weakness at the top of his armor and imbedded in his shoulder.  Ignoring the pain, Vilamil tried to move uphill so he had more of an advantage but his attacker moved with him and swung his weapons quickly keeping Vilamil at a distance. 
<br />

<br />
Somewhere in the back of his mind he was aware of a female screaming but he was too seasoned in battle to be distracted.   His attacker rushed him, with several fast hard jabs but Vilamil  countered them with his daggers.  His opponent had the advantage of size and longer reaching weapons and he kept Vilamil downhill and out of range of a back stab.  
<br />

<br />
Again Vilamil tried to move to higher ground but his opponent stubbornly refused to give up his position.  He slashed at Vilamil every time he tried to gain ground forcing the rogue to stay downhill.   Giving up his ploy to gain the high ground Vilamil started an assault of his own, moving in and out of range with a series of low jabs with his daggers.  His daggers were much faster weapons and his assailant was wearing out with the constant parries.  
<br />

<br />
He knew he could win if he could outlast the fighter.  Already his opponent was getting weary but then he felt pain as more arrows struck him.  Vilamil pressed his opponent and tried to get behind him.  The warrior slashed at him low and hard attempting to open his kneecaps with the long sword.   Instead of jumping completely out of the way, Vilamil sprang right then stabbed his dagger down on the elf's sword arm as he skipped backwards.   He felt his stab hit bone and the long sword suddenly dropped from his opponents hands as a spurt of blood shot upward.  His opponent stared and cursed at his curling fingers, frozen with numbness as Vilamil pressed in again to finish him.  
<br />

<br />
Fortunately the assailant was not as good with his off hand.  A clumsy attempt to cut off Vilamil's head left him unbalanced and Vilamil made a fatal thrust into his flesh just right of his armpit.  The warrior staggered  tried  to skewer Vilamil with the short sword but the rogue easily dodged the blow and with a stab to the back of the neck finished him.  The barrage of arrows hit him again, this time with the sweet sickly smell of Crag spider poison.  Vilamil glanced up at the ridge.  So now they were trying to paralyze him.  He was not going to fall victim to that trap.  He went searching for the nearest archer.  It was not till he'd killed two archers that the remaining two dropped their bows and fled.  Vilamil pulled out his own bow and shot them each once fatally in the back.  No one who attacked him ever lived to tell about it.
<br />

<br />
He checked their corpses for anything of value then headed back towards the path and the injured human.  A pregnant half-breed was standing in the middle of the path hovering over the injured man.  Her hands were bound in front of her and she was crying and   trying to wake him.  She stared at Vilamil in fear when she looked up and noticed him.
<br />

<br />
Vilamil regarded her indifferently.  So this is what the Nerksis were hiding.  A half-breed, no doubt on her way to Neriak for sacrifice.  He wondered if she knew what her captors had intended, then doubted it when she started speaking and gesturing very slowly to him as if she thought he couldn't understand her.
<br />

<br />
She pointed at him.  “You...saved... us.” she finished pointing at herself and the injured human.  Then she smiled and pointed at him and her.  “Half-elves.” and back at the dead tier'dal.  “Dark elves.  Evil.” she frowned.
<br />

<br />

<br />
“I understand common tongue.” he said as he walked past her and headed towards the lake.  He was feeling woozy from the poison and he wanted to clean out the wounds with the water and see if he had anything to neutralize it.  At best he'd have something and be on his way.  At worse he didn't and he'd have to hole up somewhere in Lake Rathe and wait for the poison to filter out of his system.  He swore to Innoruuk as he checked the wounds.  What were the odds he'd get attacked by the Nerksis.  He still couldn't figure out why.  Unless.  His gaze shifted back up in the direction of the mountains, the Nerksis somehow got the idea he was one of the half-breeds.  He remembered the gypsies and realized his error.  So that's what this pregnant girl meant by her comment.  She too thought he was a half breed.  He chuckled.  The Nerksis should have known by looking at him he was as Tier'dal as they were, maybe even more. 
<br />

<br />
Hearing a noise behind him he turned and saw the pregnant girl leading a pony.  She  walked up to him and looked at him nervously.  “You look hurt.  Do you want me to look at your wounds.” she said reaching towards his armor.  He pulled back and scooted away before she could touch him.  He knew he should kill her but he wasn't feeling himself.  He felt cold and his vision was blurring.   
<br />

<br />
“You're free.” he said as he slashed her bonds with his dagger.  “Go away before your captors return.”
<br />

<br />
To his horror she started crying.  Damn Females.  Vilamil didn't have the time or the patience for female hysterics.  He backed away from her even further and retreated down the bank.  She kept following.  He was ready to kill her and take her horse.  Didn't she realize he was evil.
<br />

<br />
“Please, I need  your help.  Devin is injured.”
<br />

<br />
A wave of nausea washed over him as he reached for his dagger.  Changing his mind he put his hand on his stomach instead and pressed on it to try and squelch the urge to vomit.  He was barely cognizant of her babbling.  
<br />

<br />
“I need you to help me get him up on the horse.  We can't leave him in the middle of the path, a lion could eat him.”
<br />

<br />
Vilamil ignored her.  He continued retreating till she was far behind then he looked for some sort of shelter to clean his wounds and wait out the day.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Kaldarye Ka'Duceus
