			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Bridgid and Devin Maclean delivered a healthy 8 pound baby boy in the backwoods of Qeynos Hills that they named Darone. A few days later they returned to Surefall Glade, got married and set up house near the shores of the lake. Theirs is an oft' repeated tale and if you want to hear the full version just set down on the shores of the lake next to Devin while he's fishing for dinner.  He's there every night, often using the same crude fishing pole given to him by the Dark One.   He'll give you the full version of the tale of the half elven Dark skinned ranger that rescued  them and became the babe's namesake.  
<br />

<br />
Of course not many in the Glade actually believe the tale.  Everyone know's that there is no such thing as a dark-skinned half elven ranger.  And much speculation as to the dark elf's true identity has grown.  Many think it wasn't a dark elf at all but  a ranger wearing a tier'dal illusion.  Some think he was just a human with darker skin.  Others wonder if Karana himself came to the couple's aid.  Whoever he was, Devin, Bridgid and their child owe him a debt of gratitude and claim they'll always open their doors to any friendly Tier'dal wanderers.   Not that any Tier'dal ever go to Surefall Glade, but then again you never know.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Kaldarye Ka'Duceus
<br />
Ugly Lady of the Hovel
<br />
