			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Lesser Faydark
<br />

<br />
As he ran away from the barn,  Vilamil's boots made a rhythmic staccato on the cold Karana field. His breath appeared in smoky gusts.  Though he had spent the past several days running across the Karanas with Devin, Bridgid and a pony in tow, the land beneath his feet now seemed hostile.  He became acutely aware that he was a lone dark elf in the land of the light races.  A sense of urgency entered his stride.  He wanted to be out of the Karanas before the morning sun rose, and the ranger patrols caught his scent.   He headed towards Qeynos City and the portal to knowledge.   The further he got from the pregnant half elf the less nauseous he felt; and just before sunrise when he reached the portal, the sickness vanished.  
<br />

<br />
He crossed over and stopped to catch his breath.   Plain of knowledge was more like the Plain of placidity.   The air was stagnant and unchanging except for the multitude of creatures passing through on the way to someplace more exciting.  Vilamil was no exception.   He made a brief stop at an inn for  a meal, a good nap and replenish his supplies before making his way to towards Ak'abon.  He had one last outpost to visit before he returned to Neriak to collect D'Jaren's reward. 
<br />

<br />
Ak'Abon, home to the gnomes, was a series of valleys and foothills in the shadow of the old Steamfont mountains.  Though smaller and much less dangerous than Rathe, Steamfont still had it's dangers.  Tantalizing views lured the unsuspecting.   Mountain lion and  emerald drakes prowled the trails and malfunctioning tinkered creatures waited amidst the rocks to snare the unsuspecting.     It was not a place a dark elf wanted to stay for long.
<br />

<br />
Vilamil stepped away from the portal.   It was a cold and drizzly day.   The air smelled of spruce and wild onions.  A light fog draped the mountains.  He slipped on a pair of gloves and pulled his cloak around his shoulders. 
<br />

<br />
He was the only one near the Ak'Abon portal but every thirty seconds or so could hear the guttural cry of a young gnome shouting, “Someone help me, I need buffs.  Someone give me a weapon and help me.  Someone give me platinum.”  Every time he spoke the gnome's cries carried over the hills echoing three or four times, making Vilamil wince.   “Someone help me I need buffs.”   The young gnome's voice was demanding.    
<br />

<br />
Finished putting on warmer attire, Vilamil moved away from the portal and headed towards a small copse of birch trees. The fog was unusually thick around the white trunks as if a gathering of ghosts were rehearsing a sinewy dance.  It was chilly for October and the cold air seeped past his cloak and stung the skin under his collar.   He pulled his cloak higher on his neck, tied it off, then started running towards the the nearest mountain, a Mayan gray edifice surrounded by  hundreds of boulders.   The mountain was wrapped by a rocky trail that led towards the summit.   
<br />

<br />
It took Vilamil forty minutes to climb the steep trail to a plateau where it leveled off and gently sloped down the other side.  He continued following the trail until he came to a curve where the interlocking branches of the birch and pine  formed a window to the valley.   The view was spectacular. Brown paths wound through yellow fields, themselves lying between mountains, old and overgrown.      Birch, maple, and oak dazzled his eyes with their autumn foliage.  The predominant color of the trees was orange with a smattering of red, gold and green.   He could see well into the distance.  The trail he was on followed the mountain range all the way to the evergreen forest of Lesser Faydark.    
<br />

<br />
It took him most of the day to reach the forest and then the rest of the evening to find the outpost.   When he arrived the night was quiet; the stars were competing with a light smattering of clouds.   Occasionally a dry wind stirred up the leaves but the cold sting he'd felt in the mountains was gone.   He hoped for a hot meal and a warm bed but as he looked around, his hopes were dashed.  
<br />

<br />
The outpost in Lesser Faydark was exactly that, an outpost composed of tents, fires and a few drogmar guarding the perimeter.   The tier'dal stationed here were at the behest of the Healing Temple of Neriak to observe the strange magics of Castle Mistmoore and making the occasional kill of any lightie that got too close and curious.  
<br />

<br />
They were not friendly or impressed by his N'Bane house pin.  If anything they seemed annoyed that he invaded their space.   No they hadn't seen Kaldarye, and no they weren't interested in hunting down and slaying half elves, but if one came to close they'd kill it and offer it to Innoruuk.  Vilamil spent the better part of his visit trying to convince them he was not a Nerksis and finally left after a few hours without much luck or a meal in his belly.   It was curious that these Tier'dal wanted no affiliation with the new religious movement of Neriak  but Vilamil had more important matters on his mind than the quirks of the tier'dal in Lesser Fay.   Likely they'd been tainted by the Mistmoore magic.   
<br />

<br />
He was out of Lesser Fay and on his way back to Neriak by the night's end, returning to knowledge via the portal of Greater Fay and then crossing over  to the portal of Neriak.  When he arrived in Talon Village he went straight to his private quarters to refresh himself before he made another appointment with D'jaren.   It would be interesting to see his liege's reaction when he informed there was still no trace of Kaldarye in any of the outer posts. 
<br />

<br />
Vilamil couldn't figure out why Kaldarye's whereabouts were so urgent to D'Jaren.    From his last meeting he'd detected an edge in his clan lord's voice and he really wanted to find out why he was getting paid good money to locate her.   On and off during his adventure with the human and the half-breed he had toyed with the idea of turning her in,  but  whatever reason D'Jaren had for wanting her in his house under his roof had him curious.  Maybe he'd sneak around house N'bane before he had his face to face meeting with D'Jaren.  One never knows what one might overhear...<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Kaldarye Ka'Duceus
<br />
Ugly Lady of the Hovel
<br />
Dark Mistress of Innoruuk
<br />
