			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Not wanting to deal with the feeling that just enveloped him, Vilamil walked down the corridor, through a massive set of wooden double doors that were propped open and into a large solarium.  At the edge of the solarium was another hallway that lead back towards D'jaren's private wing.
<br />

<br />
As he approached hidden entrance to the blue walled meeting room he heard two voices, D'jaren and his half brother the high priest Baellor.  They were discussing Valatha and Kaldarye.  Vilamil ducked into the shadows behind a potted fungus and listened.  He could sense agitation building in the high priest.  
<br />

<br />
“I don't approve of this match.”  Baellor said in angry tones.  
<br />

<br />
“You don't have to.  I'm the one that ordered it.”D'jaren replied cooly.
<br />

<br />
“But why do this.  Valatha is my eldest.  She's a capable courtesan.”
<br />

<br />
“Yes and a talented player at the noble's game.  Talents she learned at my expense and tutelage. It's time she put her social skills to good uses for her clan.”
<br />

<br />
Baellor's voice was mixed with fury.  “How social can she be in a commoner's household.  Her marriage is a death sentence to her access to court.”
<br />

<br />
D'jaren kept his gaze on Baellor.  “I don't need Valatha at court.  I need the attention of the court focused on her.”
<br />

<br />
“The court will be whispering about this unusual alliance.  High nobles don't marry out of their class.  The court  will think she has angered you.  It will trigger some houses to plot.  They will deuce that by taking Valatha out, it will bring your favor.”
<br />

<br />
D'Jaren shook his head.  “No one will dare attack her.  The court will know she married with my blessing and they will wonder why I approved it.   It will drive them crazy in their beds.  They will wonder what house N'bane is up to.  Their fear of me will make them seek out your daughter  for answers.” 
<br />

<br />
Baellor blinked.  His frown deepened. “And what will she tell them?”
<br />

<br />
“Nothing.”  D'jaren gave his brother a diabolical grin. “Valatha doesn't know why I am forcing her to marry into House V'Karissia.  But she is too skilled to let the court of Neriak know that.  She will delude them into believing she's privy to the answer, and in the thick of my plotting.  It will keep the peers guessing.”
<br />

<br />
“No doubt most courtiers will be talking of nothing else for weeks.” Baellor's face softened, bit by bit as he realized what his brother was up to.  His gaze grew distant and then wretched back to the face of the clanlord.  “And what does our house gain by this deception?”
<br />

<br />
“Time.”
<br />

<br />
The high priest narrowed his eyes.  “What do we need time for?”
<br />

<br />
“To find Kaldarye.”
<br />

<br />
“Your daughter?  Isn't she wallowing away in the blood temple killing the half breeds for the Nerksis.” the high priest said with derision.
<br />

<br />
D'jaren's eyes glanced away.  He looked hesitant.  “No.”  He drew his eyes back to Baellor. “She's missing.  I demanded her return to House N'bane and that fool Tramplebrey put me off to hide the fact that he doesn't have her.  For months he's tried to claim he'd gotten her with child and she's cloistered to wait out it's birth.” D'Jaren replied.
<br />

<br />
“The blood temple has many passages.  It's rumored there's a secret chamber that can't be scryed on.  How do you know she's not there.”
<br />

<br />
“I had the rogue check.”
<br />

<br />
“Vilamil?”
<br />

<br />
“Yes.” D'Jaren answered.
<br />

<br />
Baellor frowned. “I don't trust him.  Most rogues don't follow Innoruuk.”
<br />

<br />
“He is of our blood.”
<br />

<br />
“But he takes contracts to the highest bidder.  What if someone thinks his services are worth more than you do.”
<br />

<br />
“There aren't many elves that can outbid me.”  D'jaren laughed.
<br />

<br />
“I still don't trust him.  There are ways other than platinum to pay a rogue off.”
<br />

<br />
“Ways I am well familiar with, but Vilamil won't betray us.   He is clan.”
<br />

<br />
“Clan or not, your faith is misguided if he's loyal to Bristlebane.”
<br />

<br />
“You priests of hate are so touchy about anything not related to Innoruuk.   Don't worry about who Vilamil worships, his first loyalty is to me.”
<br />

<br />
Baellor pinched his lips.  “I can see this argument is pointless. I hope your trust  is not misplaced.”
<br />

<br />
“It's not.”
<br />

<br />
The high priest looked grim. “Assuming the rogue hasn't misguided you, what if you don't find your daughter?” 
<br />

<br />
“I will.  I'm using all my resources.”
<br />

<br />
“If you don't find Kaldarye,  Valatha would have been your next logical heir, and this afternoon your making her take the name V'Krissia, a commoners clan.”
<br />

<br />
“Pr'Manthis V'Krissia is not noble.  If need be he can be expended.  What's done can be undone.  But right now clan V'Krissia has it's uses.”
<br />

<br />
“How do you know Kaldarye's not dead?”
<br />

<br />
“That is a question I am beginning to wonder myself.  It is why I summoned you here.  The rogue's loyalty to me is unquestioned.  Let's see if yours is.”
<br />

<br />
Baellor lifted his brows.  “You doubt me?”
<br />

<br />
D'jaren smiled evilly.  “I have no reason to.  But since you brought up the subject of loyalty then you know I expect unfailing loyalty from all my retainers.” his gaze slid up and down his brother.
<br />

<br />
“So much trust that you'd ask me to use my inferior priestly magic over your own wizardly might.” Baellor replied using an old barb from their childhood.
<br />

<br />
D'jaren looked annoyed.  “I have scryed for Kaldarye's face everywhere.  No where is it to be found.  Now  I need you to commune to Innoruuk and tell me if my daughter still lives.”
<br />

<br />
“It takes time to commune.  I'll have to prepare an alter.” 
<br />

<br />
“Do whatever you must but get me the answer.”
<br />

<br />
“As you wish.”
<br />

<br />
“Oh and do not think of betraying me.  I will know if your lips speak truth.”  D'jaren warned.
<br />

<br />
Crouched in his hiding spot, Vilamil grew cold as the high priest left the room  He wondered if Baellor would find out that Kaldarye was in his and Greon's custody.   And if D'jaren ever found out where Kaldarye currently was,  the trust Vilamil had so carefully cultivated with this clan lord would be destroyed.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Kaldarye Ka'Duceus
<br />
Ugly Lady of the Hovel
<br />
Dark Mistress of Innoruuk
<br />
<a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=1010140" target="_blank" class="postlink">Magelo</a></div></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
