				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Vilamil waited until D'jaren left his room then he entered it and secured another hiding place behind the fungus plants on the far wall.  He waited.  He knew he should leave and get Kaldarye out of Greon's house, perhaps even claim he'd found her in one of the various outposts and return her to house N'bane but he had to find out what Innoruuk betrayed to Baellor.  D'Jaren's brother was not of the Blood Temple nor the Healing temple; he'd formed his own temple and sect of Innoruuk's faith within the village of Talon, but that didn't mean he lacked Innoruuk's favor.  In fact the opposite was the case as the church in Talon focused on some of the darker more sinister side of hate.  Vilamil knew that returning to Talon House with Kaldarye in tow when D'jaren knew of his betrayal would be foolish.  He couldn't risk that, but neither could her risk not knowing if  his clanlord's trust had been destroyed.   Hours passed before D'jaren and Baellor returned.  
<br />

<br />
 He could see that the high priest looked grim.
<br />

<br />
“Well, what have you learned.”  D'jaren demanded.
<br />

<br />
“Kaldarye is not dead.”  Baellor replied.  He paused and looked as if he'd give anything not to continue but at D'jaren's frown added.  “But neither can I figure out where she is.”
<br />

<br />
“Innoruuk's testicles.” D'jaren swore.  He paced the room.  “Where could she have hidden herself.”
<br />

<br />
“Only Innoruuk knows.  Your daughter is strong with Hate.  If Innoruuk wants her hidden there is little we can do to find her.”
<br />

<br />
D'jaren's frosty eyes snapped to his brother.  Exasperated he said, “That's not acceptable.  I need her brought here to this house, now.”
<br />

<br />
Baellor's dark eyes roamed his brother's face as he toyed with his unholy symbol of Innoruuk in one hand.  He chose his words carefully.  “To find her we would have to gain more favor with Innoruuk than she has.  I'm not sure we can.  It is rumored she is marked.”
<br />

<br />
“She is not marked.  Her contract to House Ka'Duceus is.”  D'jaren replied.
<br />

<br />
Baellor lifted a brow.  “Then she's bound to it by Innoruuk's hand.  You still wish to undo it?”
<br />

<br />
“There are ways.” D'jaren replied vaguely with a nod of his head.
<br />

<br />
Baellor looked uneasy.   He had seen what happened when D'jaren didn't get his way.  And the thought of helping his brother get what he wanted against Innoruuk's will made him wary.  “May I ask why you want to see your daughter now when for years you've been disgusted by the sight of her?”
<br />

<br />
“It's not me that wants to see her.  It's Thex that wants to see her.”
<br />

<br />
“The king?”
<br />

<br />
“Yes the king.” D'jaren replied as he curled his fingers into a ball.  The vein at his temple throbbed as he struggled to control his fury.  For a moment he held perfectly still.  His blue eyes, so like Kaldarye, focused on the wall.  Then slowly he lifted his hand and pointed his finger at the hearth and unleashed a firely bolt of pale blue lightening.   The flames rose higher and exploded into a small fireball that twisted into a column of smoke and blasted up the flue.
<br />

<br />
From his hiding place, Vilamil was momentarily stunned.  <span style="font-style: italic">The king</span>!    He held his breath.  His eyes locked on D'Jaren through the smokey haze.  No wonder his clan lord was so intent on finding her.  With Thex at his door, D'jaren was using every trick he knew to hold their leader off.   The wedding of Valatha to a commoner was just a smoke screen and a diversion.   Vilamil thought back on all the recent events in Neriak that had transpired.  Why was the king  interested in Kaldarye?  The reason was surely worth a small fortune.  In his mind Vilamil calculated what D'Jaren would pay to have Kaldarye back at Talon House.  Fifty thousand?  One hundred thousand?  The money would be useful.  There were a few items he had his eye on in the bazaar, but before he could get too excited, a frown crossed his face.  In his mind he envisioned Kaldarye as she looked now.  Her face was so mangled that D'Jaren wouldn't recognize her much less take her to the king.  She'd be rejected by all of Neriak if her marred features became public.  Hopefully Greon could repair the damage.  Vilamil was counting on it.  He smiled to himself,  if Greon did a good job he'd even pay him for his efforts, a small reward left anonymously.
<br />

<br />

<br />
“Innoruuk's hate, why is the king interested in Kaldarye?”  Baellor looked aghast.
<br />

<br />
Still looking at the grate and the waning explosion D'jaren replied, “Because of that foul creature she married.”
<br />

<br />
“Greon?”
<br />

<br />
D'jaren's eyes blazed.  “Don't mention his name to me.”
<br />

<br />
“Greon is a pauper and a peasant.  Why should anything he does interest the king.”  Baellor replied mentioning the forbidden name again.
<br />

<br />
“He is far from a peasant.  His house is of old lineage.”
<br />

<br />
“A dead lineage.  His line is forgotton.”
<br />

<br />
“Not anymore.”  D'Jaren continued.  “House Ka'Duceus attended Court last week. That slut Arimelle leaked a rumor that House Ka'Duceus was allied to Talon House via marriage.” 
<br />

<br />
“A rumor that can be easily put down, m'Lord”  Baellor replied.
<br />

<br />
“Not so easily when tis true.”
<br />

<br />
“But Kaldarye married without your consent or knowledge, surely that makes  the match inconsequential.”
<br />

<br />
“Far from it.  The Seal of the Council of the Arch Fiend is on their contract.  I know because I tried to have it annulled.”  D'Jaren was fuming.  “And because Her husband has thrown his support publicly behind Punox; it is assumed that I have thrown my support behind Punox as well.  Mine is the greater house, I cannot contradict the lesser house my daughter has allied Talon too or it will look as if I can't control my underlings or my heir.”
<br />

<br />
“Perhaps you should send Greon a warning.” Baellor replied. 
<br />

<br />
D'jaren, turned, met Baellor's gaze and nodded.  His pale blue eyes glowed with malice.  “If Kaldarye doesn't turn up soon.  I will.”<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br />Kaldarye Ka'Duceus
<br />
Ugly Lady of the Hovel
<br />
Dark Mistress of Innoruuk
<br />
